## P0.5 — VPS handoff verification  ← START HERE on the VPS
- [ ] `corepack enable && pnpm install` on the VPS (check Node ≥ 22: `node -v`)
- [ ] `pnpm infra:up` → postgres/redis/minio/mailpit healthy (`docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.yml ps`)
- [ ] `cp .env.example apps/api/.env` → `pnpm --filter @poyalo/api prisma:migrate` (first real run of the init migration; fix it if it fails)
- [ ] `pnpm --filter @poyalo/api doctor` → ✔ postgres, postgis, redis
- [ ] `pnpm --filter @poyalo/api dev` → `curl 127.0.0.1:3000/health/ready` returns 200
- [ ] `docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.yml --profile app up -d --build` → api container healthy
- [ ] Check GitHub Actions ran on the push. Fix CI (format, migrate, drift check, openapi freshness) until green
- [ ] Optional: `bash infra/osrm/prepare.sh` + osrm profile (check VPS RAM first, ≥ 8 GB for southern-zone)
- [ ] Remove the ⚠ marks above once verified; log results in memory/SESSION_LOG.md

